/* 073 */             new java.util.Date(primitive4 * 1000L)));
/* 074 */       } catch (java.lang.Throwable e) {
/* 075 */         isNull0 = true;
/* 076 */       }
/* 077 */     }
```

Similarly Calendar.getInstance was used in DateTimeUtils which can be lazily inited.
## How was this patch tested?

org.apache.spark.sql.catalyst.expressions.DateExpressionsSuite,org.apache.spark.sql.catalyst.util.DateTimeUtilsSuite
Also tried with couple of sample SQL queries with single executor (6GB) which showed good improvement with the fix.

## What changes were proposed in this pull request?

This PR adds support for generating the `AggregateHashMap` class in `TungstenAggregate` if the aggregate group by keys/value are of `LongType`. Note that currently this generate aggregate is not actually used.

NB: This currently only supports `LongType` keys/values (please see `isAggregateHashMapSupported` in `TungstenAggregate`) and will be generalized to other data types in a subsequent PR.
